nvestigation (E003)**. If immature, HLR-5 is deferred and its epic does not exist this release → gated main-plan epic with `remove` impact. |\n58\t\n59\tNo other unknowns appear in the strategy (no risks table, assumptions, pending\n60\treviews, or conditional ADRs are present). Implementation details the strategy\n61\tleaves open (exact quota provisioning model, Dashboard view layout, preemption\n62\tpolicy schema) are captured as acceptance criteria on the relevant epics, not\n63\tflagged.\n64\t\n65\t## Epic List (main plan)\n66\t\n67\t| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n68\t|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n69\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E001 | Validate Kueue gang admission for multi-node training jobs at target scale | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n70\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E002 | Determine required preemption semantics for training workloads | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n71\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E003 | Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n72\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 | Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n73\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E005 | Surface queue position, quota consumption, and admission state in the Dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 | Implement admin-defined preemption policy for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n75\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 | Implement topology-aware GPU placement preference | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n76\t\n77\t### Conditional branch epics (gated by E001, not standalone Jira issues)\n78\t\n79\t| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n80\t|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n81\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008 | Enable all-or-nothing gang admission using Kueue as-is (HLR-1) | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n82\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008 | Implement gang admission with scheduler-plugin coscheduling (HLR-1) | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n83\t\n84\t## Dependency DAG\n85\t\n86\t```mermaid\n87\tgraph TD\n88\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: gang admission viability (P0)\"]\n89\t    E002[\"E002 Investigation: preemption semantics (P1)\"]\n90\t    E003[\"E003 Investigation: topology discovery maturity (P2)\"]\n91\t    E004[\"E004 Implementation: per-project GPU quota (P0)\"]\n92\t    E005[\"E005 Implementation: Dashboard queue/quota visibility (P1)\"]\n93\t    E006[\"E006 Implementation: preemption policy (P1)\"]\n94\t    E007[\"E007 Implementation: topology-aware placement (P2)\"]\n95\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E008: gang admission via Kueue (P0)\"]\n96\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E008: gang admission via scheduler-plugin (P0)\"]\n97\t\n98\t    E001 --> BA\n99\t    E001 --> BB\n100\t    E002 --> E006\n101\t    E003 --> E007\n102\t    E001 --> E007\n103\t    E004 --> E005\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\tArrows point from dependency to dependent (\"E001 --> E006\" means E001 must\n107\tcomplete before E006 starts). Branch epics (dashed conceptually) hang off the\n108\tE001 investigation and are not main-plan nodes.\n109\t\n110\t## DAG Justification\n111\t\n112\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n113\t|------|------|-----------|\n114\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Gang-admission viability determines whether HLR-1 is configuration-only (branch A). True gate: `rewrite` — if Kueue proves insufficient this scope is subsumed into scheduler-plugin work. |\n115\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E008 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Same investigation, opposite outcome: scheduler-plugin work exists only if Kueue is insufficient. True gate: `remove` if Kueue suffices. |\n116\t| E002 → E006 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Preemption semantics investigation rewrites the preemption epic's scope (full eviction vs checkpoint-aware). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n117\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Topology-discovery maturity decides whether HLR-5 ships this release. True gate: `remove` (defer to later release). |\n118\t| E001 → E007 | Rule 3 / Rule 12 | Topology-aware placement is scheduling-level work that builds on whichever admission/scheduling mechanism the gang-admission investigation selects; it cannot start before that decision. |\n119\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The Dashboard surfaces queue position, quota consumption, and admission state produced by the quota/admission enforcement capability; it is a consumer of that work. Dashboard reads the existing Kueue Workload CR and metrics interfaces (per architecture context), which are stable across both E001 outcomes, so no dependency on the branch work is modeled (main-plan epics cannot depend on branch epics). |\n120\t| (no edge) E001 → E004 | Rule 3 decision rule, applied per downstream work | Kueue's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model is GA (architecture context) and enforces quota at admission time regardless of the gang-scheduling mechanism; the investigation outcome does not change what the quota epic does. Kept parallel so HLR-2 delivers independent partial value. |\n121\t| (no edge) E004 ∥ E001, E002 ∥ E003, E004 ∥ E002/E003 | Rule 14 | Independent investigations and independent implementation work in the same component area run in parallel; no shared build artifact. |\n122\t\n123\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n124\t\n125\t| HLR | Priority | Covered by |\n126\t|-----|----------|------------|\n127\t| HLR-1 (all-or-nothing gang admission) | P0 | BRANCH-A-E008 (outcome A) / BRANCH-B-E008 (outcome B); unknown resolved by E001 |\n128\t| HLR-2 (per-project GPU quota at admission) | P0 | E004 |\n129\t| HLR-3 (Dashboard queue/quota/admission visibility) | P1 | E005 |\n130\t| HLR-4 (admin-defined preemption policy) | P1 | E002 (resolves semantics) + E006 |\n131\t| HLR-5 (topology-aware placement preference) | P2 | E003 (resolves maturity) + E007 |\n132\t\n133\tAll five HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n134\t\n135\t## Branch Decomposition\n136\t\n137\t**E001 bounded outcomes (≤3):**\n138\t\n139\t- **Branch A — Kueue sufficient**: `waitForPodsReady` all-or-nothing semantics\n140\t  hold for PyTorchJob and RayJob at target scale. HLR-1 is delivered by\n141\t  configuring/enabling Kueue gang admission for training workload classes\n142\t  (BRANCH-A-E008). Gate failure impact: `rewrite` — configuration-only scope is\n143\t  subsumed into the scheduler-plugin implementation.\n144\t- **Branch B — scheduler-plugin required**: Kueue semantics insufficient.\n145\t  HLR-1 requires scheduler-plugin (e.g. coscheduling) work beyond Kueue,\n146\t  integrated with Kueue quota (BRANCH-B-E008). Gate failure impact: `remove` —\n147\t  if Kueue suffices, this work is unnecessary.\n148\t\n149\tBoth branch epics carry `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9005-E001`, and\n150\t`gate_failure_impact` frontmatter; E001 is in each branch epic's\n151\t`dependencies`. No main-plan epic lists a branch epic in its dependencies.\n152\t\n153\t## Health Warnings\n154\t\n155\t- **Missing strategy sections**: no Acceptance Criteria, no Dependencies\n156\t  table, no Impacted Teams table, no NFRs (see Strategy Parsing Notes). Epic\n157\t  acceptance criteria below were derived from HLRs and the problem statement;\n158\t  a human should confirm they match intent.\n159\t- **Component change detail absent**: the Affected Components list gives no\n160\t  per-component change descriptions. Training Operator was classified passive\n161\t  based on architecture context (admission flows through Kueue integration);\n162\t  if the gang-admission investigation (branch B) reveals operator-side changes\n163\t  are needed, a Training Operator epic should be added inside that branch.\n164\t- **Priority consistency**: no inversions found — P0 admission/quota work is\n165\t  gated by a P0 investigation; P1/P2 features are gated by same-priority\n166\t  investigations.\n167\t- **Scope trap (minor)**: HLR-5 depends on a Tech Preview capability; the\n168\t  decomposition deliberately gates it on a maturity investigation rather than\n169\t  assuming the Tech Preview API is buildable, to avoid ACs implying\n170\t  infrastructure that may not be supported.\n171\t\n172\t## Tiered Delivery\n173\t\n174\tNo external dependency with uncertain timing exists (all uncertainty is\n175\tinternal and modeled as investigation gates). Partial value still flows:\n176\tHLR-2 (quota enforcement) and HLR-3 (Dashboard visibility) proceed in parallel\n177\twith the gang-admission investigation, so the strategy delivers\n178\tquota-enforcement and visibility value even while HLR-1's approach is being\n179\tresolved.\n180\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83032d737c0b56b2","agent_id":"a1e0061ee79c52f80","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"cbc0922d-b50b-4b40-bfff-78db93d2f725","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:23:29.609Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-adf36a6672639671","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
