commendation states which preemption semantics (full eviction\n50\t  with requeue, checkpoint-aware graceful preemption, or a policy-configurable\n51\t  mix) the admin-defined preemption policy must support, with rationale.\n52\t- The checkpoint-overhead benchmark results are documented and support the\n53\t  recommendation.\n54\t- Any policy options that must remain admin-configurable are enumerated.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-4 (P1, higher-priority workloads preempt lower-priority ones per\n59\t  admin-defined policy) — resolves the unknown that determines the scope of\n60\t  the preemption policy implementation.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83032d737c0b56b2","agent_id":"a1e0061ee79c52f80","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"c3b6812f-f6fd-4c3f-9a3f-2601f10eb2fa","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:23:33.242Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a11bfa9d8bad3bc3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
