{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4e547372893a7dc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E006\n3\ttitle: Implement admin-defined preemption policy for training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation selects checkpoint-aware graceful preemption\n15\t    instead of full eviction with requeue, the implementation scope is rewritten to\n16\t    include checkpoint orchestration; the epic exists under either outcome\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Implement admin-defined preemption policy for training workloads\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplements preemption of lower-priority training workloads by\n39\thigher-priority ones according to an admin-defined policy, with the preemption\n40\tsemantics (full eviction with requeue vs. checkpoint-aware graceful\n41\tpreemption) determined by the completed investigation into customer\n42\trequirements and checkpoint overhead.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Implement preemption of lower-priority training workloads when\n47\t  higher-priority workloads need their resources, driven by an admin-defined\n48\t  policy.\n49\t- Support the preemption semantics the completed requirements investigation\n50\t  selected (full eviction with requeue, checkpoint-aware graceful preemption,\n51\t  or a policy-configurable mix).\n52\t- Requeue preempted jobs so they resume when capacity is available (per the\n53\t  selected semantics).\n54\t- Validate preemption behavior for PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A higher-priority workload can preempt a lower-priority one per the\n59\t  admin-defined policy, on a cluster with the queueing layer managing\n60\t  training workloads.\n61\t- Preempted jobs are handled per the selected semantics: evicted and\n62\t  requeued, or gracefully checkpointed and requeued, as determined by the\n63\t  preemption-semantics investigation.\n64\t- The policy is admin-configurable; default behavior is documented.\n65\t- Preemption works for both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads.\n66\t- Build pipeline for the affected midstream repository is green.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-4 (P1, higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones\n71\t  according to an admin-defined policy) — implementation coverage; the\n72\t  semantics decision is resolved by the gating investigation.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83032d737c0b56b2","agent_id":"a1e0061ee79c52f80","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"d74f187f-f0ea-44fe-b0db-17a1e4d204f8","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:23:38.302Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4e547372893a7dc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
