{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b612d5f8d9aab474","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E007\n3\ttitle: Implement topology-aware GPU placement preference\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If Tech Preview node topology discovery is not mature enough\n16\t    this release, HLR-5 placement preference is deferred to a later release and this\n17\t    epic does not run\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Implement topology-aware GPU placement preference\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tImplements placement preference so multi-node training jobs land on\n40\tGPU-topology-aligned nodes (avoiding, e.g., placements that cross NVLink\n41\tdomains with significant throughput loss) when the cluster exposes topology\n42\tinformation. Gated on two completed investigations: confirmation of the\n43\tadmission/scheduling mechanism for all-or-nothing admission, and confirmation\n44\tthat node topology discovery is mature enough to build on this release.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Add a placement preference for training workloads toward\n49\t  GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster exposes topology information.\n50\t- Build on the node topology discovery capability (currently Tech Preview)\n51\t  only after its maturity investigation confirms it is supported for this\n52\t  release.\n53\t- Integrate with the admission/scheduling mechanism selected by the\n54\t  gang-admission investigation, so topology preference composes with\n55\t  all-or-nothing admission and quota enforcement.\n56\t- Jobs on clusters without topology information continue to schedule normally\n57\t  (preference is best-effort, per HLR-5's \"when the cluster exposes topology\n58\t  information\").\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- On a cluster exposing topology information, a multi-node training job is\n63\t  preferentially placed on topology-aligned nodes rather than crossing\n64\t  topology domains, when such placement is feasible.\n65\t- On a cluster without topology information, jobs schedule without error and\n66\t  without topology preference.\n67\t- Placement preference composes with all-or-nothing admission: a job is not\n68\t  partially admitted to achieve better topology alignment.\n69\t- Build pipeline for the affected midstream repository is green.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-5 (P2, job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n74\t  cluster exposes topology information) — implementation coverage; whether it\n75\t  ships this release is resolved by the topology-discovery maturity\n76\t  investigation.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83032d737c0b56b2","agent_id":"a1e0061ee79c52f80","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"e088293b-92a5-4049-b466-ec1fbf1bf856","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:23:38.898Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b612d5f8d9aab474","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
