under either outcome) is defensible under Rule 3, noted\n33\t    for modeling consistency only.\n34\terror: null\n35\t---\n36\t## Review Summary\n37\t\n38\tScore: 11/14 — fail\n39\tRecommendation: revise\n40\t\n41\tPass/fail note: the total score clears the pass threshold, but Criterion 4\n42\t(Type Correctness) scores 0 due to a major gating-metadata defect. Per the\n43\tauto-fail rule, any criterion at 0 forces `pass: false`.\n44\t\n45\t## Criterion Details\n46\t\n47\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n48\t\n49\tAll five HLRs are covered and the traceability matrix is present and complete:\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 (P0): E001 resolves the unknown; BRANCH-A-E008 / BRANCH-B-E008 implement it under the two bounded outcomes.\n52\t- HLR-2 (P0): E004.\n53\t- HLR-3 (P1): E005.\n54\t- HLR-4 (P1): E002 (resolves semantics) + E006 (implements).\n55\t- HLR-5 (P2): E003 (resolves maturity) + E007 (implements).\n56\t\n57\tPriority inheritance is correct: E001 is P0 (it gates all HLR-1 work), E002 is\n58\tP1 (gates HLR-4), E003 is P2 (gates HLR-5). No epic has a prerequisite of\n59\tlower priority than the work it enables. No priority collapse: every epic maps\n60\tto exactly one HLR, so no deferrable lower-priority feature is bundled with\n61\tP0 work. Triage is absent (full decomposition), so multi-epic output is\n62\texpected and correct.\n63\t\n64\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n65\t\n66\tDiagram/frontmatter cross-check passes in both directions. Diagram edges\n67\t(E001→BA, E001→BB, E002→E006, E003→E007, E001→E007, E004→E005) exactly match\n68\tthe `dependencies` lists of the target epics (E005:[E004], E006:[E002],\n69\tE007:[E001,E003], BA:[E001], BB:[E001]); all other epics have no\n70\tdependencies. Arrows run dependency → dependent as required. No cycles. No\n71\tedge references a nonexistent epic.\n72\t\n73\tBranch handling is correct: both branch files set `branch` (A/B, matching\n74\tfilenames) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001`, and no main-plan epic lists a\n75\tbranch epic in its