onsumers that detect gates from\n137\t`gated_by`/`dependencies` will miss the E001 gate on E007.\n138\t\n139\tAll other gating metadata is correct: E006 (gated_by E002, rewrite with\n140\taction + fallback), E007's E003 gate (remove with fallback), and both branch\n141\tepics (gated_by E001 with rewrite/remove impacts) are properly populated, and\n142\tevery `gated_by` target appears in the corresponding epic's direct\n143\t`dependencies`.\n144\t\n145\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n146\t\n147\tSignal-set usage is correct throughout: all six Implementation epics\n148\t(E004–E007, both branches) carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric); all three\n149\tInvestigation epics (E001–E003) carry `investigation_signals` (5-signal\n150\trubric). No mixing. All nine ai-signals rationale files exist, and the\n151\trationales match the frontmatter values.\n152\t\n153\tOne borderline value:\n154\t\n155\t**E001 `source_accessibility: 1` is arguable.** The +1 condition requires a\n156\treadable artifact that contains or *determines* the answer. E001's gating\n157\tquestion is whether Kueue's gang admission holds *at target scale* — and the\n158\tepic's own `cluster_hardware_dependence: -2` rationale concedes that \"source\n159\tconfirms intent, not behavior under load.\" Kueue source/docs determine the\n160\tsemantics but not the empirical at-scale answer, so the decisive input is not\n161\tfully readable. The value is defensible (documented semantics and known\n162\tlimitations are readable and constrain the answer) but sits right on the\n163\tborderline; if the intent is that the skill resolves only the desk-research\n164\tportion, 0 would be the more conservative score.\n165\t\n166\tAll other signal values are well justified against the rubric and the\n167\tstrategy content (e.g., E002 `source_accessibility: 0` / `human_judgment_required: -2`\n168\tfor the customer-decision question; BRANCH-B-E008 `repo_access: 0` /\n169\t`external_dependency: -1` / `architecture_claims: