*. If immature, HLR-5 is deferred and its epic does not exist this release → gated main-plan epic with `remove` impact. |\n57\t\n58\tNo other unknowns appear in the strategy (no risks table, assumptions, pending\n59\treviews, or conditional ADRs are present). Implementation details the strategy\n60\tleaves open (exact quota provisioning model, Dashboard view layout, preemption\n61\tpolicy schema) are captured as acceptance criteria on the relevant epics, not\n62\tflagged.\n63\t\n64\t## Epic List (main plan)\n65\t\n66\t| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n67\t|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n68\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E001 | Validate Kueue gang admission for multi-node training jobs at target scale | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n69\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E002 | Determine required preemption semantics for training workloads | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n70\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E003 | Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n71\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 | Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n72\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E005 | Surface queue position, quota consumption, and admission state in the Dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n73\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 | Implement admin-defined preemption policy for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 | Implement topology-aware GPU placement preference | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n75\t\n76\t### Conditional branch epics (gated by E001, not standalone Jira issues)\n77\t\n78\t| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n79\t|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n80\t|