-4 (admin-defined preemption policy) | P1 | E002 (resolves semantics) + E006 |\n130\t| HLR-5 (topology-aware placement preference) | P2 | E003 (resolves maturity) + E007 |\n131\t\n132\tAll five HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n133\t\n134\t## Branch Decomposition\n135\t\n136\t**E001 bounded outcomes (≤3):**\n137\t\n138\t- **Branch A — Kueue sufficient**: `waitForPodsReady` all-or-nothing semantics\n139\t  hold for PyTorchJob and RayJob at target scale. HLR-1 is delivered by\n140\t  configuring/enabling Kueue gang admission for training workload classes\n141\t  (BRANCH-A-E008). Gate failure impact: `rewrite` — configuration-only scope is\n142\t  subsumed into the scheduler-plugin implementation.\n143\t- **Branch B — scheduler-plugin required**: Kueue semantics insufficient.\n144\t  HLR-1 requires scheduler-plugin (e.g. coscheduling) work beyond Kueue,\n145\t  integrated with Kueue quota (BRANCH-B-E008). Gate failure impact: `remove` —\n146\t  if Kueue suffices, this work is unnecessary.\n147\t\n148\tBoth branch epics carry `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9005-E001`, and\n149\t`gate_failure_impact` frontmatter; E001 is in each branch epic's\n150\t`dependencies`. No main-plan epic lists a branch epic in its dependencies.\n151\t\n152\t## Health Warnings\n153\t\n154\t- **Missing strategy sections**: no Acceptance Criteria, no Dependencies\n155\t  table, no Impacted Teams table, no NFRs (see Strategy Parsing Notes). Epic\n156\t  acceptance criteria below were derived from HLRs and the problem statement;\n157\t  a human should confirm they match intent.\n158\t- **Component change detail absent**: the Affected Components list gives no\n159\t  per-component change descriptions. Training Operator was classified passive\n160\t  based on architecture context (admission flows through Kueue integration);\n161\t  if the gang-admission investigation (branch B) reveals operator-side changes\n162\t  are needed, a Training Operator epic should be added inside that branch.\n163\t- **Priority consistency**: no inversions found — P0 admission/quota work is\n164\t  gated by a P0 investigation; P1/P2 features are gated by same-priority\n165\t  investigations.\n166\t- **Scope trap (minor)**: HLR-5 depends on a Tech Preview capability; the\n167\t  decomposition deliberately gates it on a maturity investigation rather than\n168\t  assuming the Tech Preview API is buildable, to avoid ACs implying\n169\t  infrastructure that may not be supported.\n170\t\n171\t## Tiered Delivery\n172\t\n173\tNo external dependency with uncertain timing exists (all uncertainty is\n174\tinternal and modeled as investigation gates). Partial value still flows:\n175\tHLR-2 (quota enforcement) and HLR-3 (Dashboard visibility) proceed in parallel\n176\twith the gang-admission investigation, so the strategy delivers\n177\tquota-enforcement and visibility value even while HLR-1's approach is being\n178\tresolved.\n179\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-848d2e3aeea8b5ab","agent_id":"aa1173200b73ff1c1","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"868c8b3d-5088-475d-aa0c-6b8ccb00ea66","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:37:32.526Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-afcd56956fc87f40","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
