{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abbb2ab3b9104413","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n3\ttitle: Determine required preemption semantics for training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Determine required preemption semantics for training workloads\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves which preemption semantics reference customers actually need for\n30\thigher-priority workloads preempting lower-priority training jobs: full\n31\teviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware graceful preemption. The strategy\n32\treports conflicting field signals and no benchmark of checkpoint overhead, and\n33\tthe answer rewrites the scope of the preemption policy implementation.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Collect and reconcile the conflicting field signals from reference\n38\t  customers regarding preemption expectations.\n39\t- Benchmark checkpoint overhead for representative multi-node training jobs\n40\t  (time to checkpoint, time to restart from checkpoint, net throughput loss vs.\n41\t  restart-from-scratch).\n42\t- Determine whether full eviction with requeue is acceptable or whether\n43\t  checkpoint-aware graceful preemption is required, and under what conditions.\n44\t- Produce a recommendation with the evidence needed to scope the\n45\t  admin-defined preemption policy work.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A written recommendation states which preemption semantics (full eviction\n50\t  with requeue, checkpoint-aware graceful preemption, or a policy-configurable\n51\t  mix) the admin-defined preemption policy must support, with rationale.\n52\t- The checkpoint-overhead benchmark results are documented and support the\n53\t  recommendation.\n54\t- Any policy options that must remain admin-configurable are enumerated.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-4 (P1, higher-priority workloads preempt lower-priority ones per\n59\t  admin-defined policy) — resolves the unknown that determines the scope of\n60\t  the preemption policy implementation.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-848d2e3aeea8b5ab","agent_id":"aa1173200b73ff1c1","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"7b8af235-562b-4133-8ce0-56bff470ac0d","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:02:18.536Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-abbb2ab3b9104413","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
