g layer so quota enforcement and queue\n51\t  accounting continue to function with the scheduler plugin in place.\n52\t- Cover the failure modes from the problem statement: partial GPU occupation\n53\t  while waiting for remaining pods, and partially scheduled jobs dying on\n54\t  timeout.\n55\t- Validate at the target scale established by the gang-admission\n56\t  investigation, including contention scenarios.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A 16-GPU-class multi-node training job holds zero GPUs while waiting for\n61\t  its remaining pods; pods are created only when the full job can be admitted.\n62\t- Both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads are admitted all-or-nothing.\n63\t- Jobs that cannot be fully admitted within the configured timeout are not\n64\t  left partially scheduled.\n65\t- Per-project quota enforcement at admission continues to function with the\n66\t  scheduler plugin active.\n67\t- Validation at target scale (per the gating investigation's scale\n68\t  definition) confirms the behavior, including under contention.\n69\t- Build pipeline for the affected midstream repository is green.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 (P0, multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing) — fully\n74\t  covered by this epic under outcome B.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-848d2e3aeea8b5ab","agent_id":"aa1173200b73ff1c1","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"1eb90c1c-e239-4ed8-9afd-2fa32a141e55","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:06:33.651Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-96c9c5a997f3b77e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
