estigation edges) | Preemption semantics investigation rewrites the preemption epic's scope (full eviction vs checkpoint-aware). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n116\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Topology-discovery maturity decides whether HLR-5 ships this release. True gate: `remove` (defer to later release). |\n117\t| (no edge) E001 → E007 | Rule 3 decision rule, applied per downstream work (removed in revision) | Topology-aware placement composes with whichever admission/scheduling mechanism is selected — the placement-preference capability is scheduler-level and mechanism-independent, mirroring the quota epic's outcome-independence argument. Mechanism composition is enforced by an acceptance criterion on the placement epic (\"composes with all-or-nothing admission under either mechanism\"), not a blocking edge; E007 is gated only by the topology-discovery maturity investigation (E003). |\n118\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The Dashboard surfaces queue position, quota consumption, and admission state produced by the quota/admission enforcement capability; it is a consumer of that work. Dashboard reads the existing Kueue Workload CR and metrics interfaces (per architecture context), which are stable across both E001 outcomes, so no dependency on the branch work is modeled (main-plan epics cannot depend on branch epics). |\n119\t| (no edge) E001 → E004 | Rule 3 decision rule, applied per downstream work | Kueue's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model is GA (architecture context) and enforces quota at admission time regardless of the gang-scheduling mechanism; the investigation outcome does not change what the quota epic does. Kept parallel so HLR-2 delivers independent partial value. |\n120\t| (no edge) E004 ∥ E001, E002 ∥ E003, E004 ∥ E002/E003 | Rule 14 | Independent investigations and independent implementation work in the same component area run in parallel; no shared build artifact. |\n121\t\n122\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n123\t\n1