ponents list gives no\n159\t  per-component change descriptions. Training Operator was classified passive\n160\t  based on architecture context (admission flows through Kueue integration);\n161\t  if the gang-admission investigation (branch B) reveals operator-side changes\n162\t  are needed, a Training Operator epic should be added inside that branch.\n163\t- **Priority consistency**: no inversions found — P0 admission/quota work is\n164\t  gated by a P0 investigation; P1/P2 features are gated by same-priority\n165\t  investigations.\n166\t- **Scope trap (minor)**: HLR-5 depends on a Tech Preview capability; the\n167\t  decomposition deliberately gates it on a maturity investigation rather than\n168\t  assuming the Tech Preview API is buildable, to avoid ACs implying\n169\t  infrastructure that may not be supported.\n170\t\n171\t## Tiered Delivery\n172\t\n173\tNo external dependency with uncertain timing exists (all uncertainty is\n174\tinternal and modeled as investigation gates). Partial value still flows:\n175\tHLR-2 (quota enforcement) and HLR-3 (Dashboard visibility) proceed in parallel\n176\twith the gang-admission investigation, so the strategy delivers\n177\tquota-enforcement and visibility value even while HLR-1's approach is being\n178\tresolved.\n179\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b01eb154d8d767e0","agent_id":"ae8a577ef2f9405e6","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"6b9f133f-9f48-4dc8-8cc6-c8fe797ffd6a","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:11:42.376Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-961863f8d1bda5de","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
