{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-887ac523fd6da274","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate Kueue gang admission for multi-node training jobs at target scale\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate Kueue gang admission for multi-node training jobs at target scale\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves whether Kueue's current gang-admission semantics (all-or-nothing\n30\tadmission via `waitForPodsReady`) satisfy the requirement that multi-node\n31\ttraining jobs are admitted all-or-nothing for PyTorchJob and RayJob at the\n32\ttarget scale, or whether scheduler-plugin work (e.g. coscheduling) beyond\n33\tKueue is required. The strategy explicitly flags that the answer changes the\n34\tshape of most of the implementation work for admission.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Establish the target scale (job sizes, GPU counts, concurrent pending\n39\t  workloads) that gang admission must hold at.\n40\t- Exercise Kueue's existing all-or-nothing admission for PyTorchJob and\n41\t  RayJob workloads at that scale, including the failure modes from the problem\n42\t  statement: partial GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods, and\n43\t  partially scheduled jobs dying on timeout.\n44\t- Characterize behavior under contention (multiple large jobs pending against\n45\t  limited GPU capacity).\n46\t- Produce a decision with evidence: Kueue as-is is sufficient, or the specific\n47\t  gap that requires scheduler-plugin work.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A written decision artifact records, with reproducible evidence, whether\n52\t  Kueue's gang admission satisfies all-or-nothing admission for PyTorchJob and\n53\t  RayJob at target scale, or identifies the specific shortfall.\n54\t- The evidence covers both job types and includes contention scenarios where\n55\t  multiple large jobs are pending simultaneously.\n56\t- The named outcome (Kueue sufficient / scheduler-plugin required) selects one\n57\t  of the two documented conditional branches for the all-or-nothing admission\n58\t  implementation.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-1 (P0, all-or-nothing admission) — resolves the unknown that determines\n63\t  how HLR-1 is implemented. The implementation of HLR-1 itself lives in the\n64\t  conditional branch epics selected by this investigation's outcome.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b01eb154d8d767e0","agent_id":"ae8a577ef2f9405e6","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"97520c2d-c6c2-45da-9ef3-4b49252e2053","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:11:46.424Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-887ac523fd6da274","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
