{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a344af813b4db132","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n3\ttitle: Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission for training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tgated_by: null\n11\tgate_failure_impact: null\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 5\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission for training workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDelivers per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time across training\n34\tjob types (PyTorchJob, RayJob), so that a project's pending and admitted\n35\ttraining workloads cannot exceed its GPU quota. Built on the platform's\n36\texisting queueing layer (Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model), which is\n37\tGA per architecture context and enforces quota at admission regardless of\n38\twhich gang-scheduling mechanism is selected for all-or-nothing admission.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define and provision per-project GPU quota for training job types\n43\t  (PyTorchJob, RayJob) using the queueing layer's quota model.\n44\t- Enforce quota at admission time: jobs that would exceed the project's GPU\n45\t  quota are held pending rather than partially admitted.\n46\t- Cover both training job types named in the strategy.\n47\t- Validate that PyTorchJob workloads continue to be admitted through the\n48\t  existing queueing integration with quota enforced (passive-component\n49\t  validation for the Training Operator).\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A project with an admitted training job consuming most of its GPU quota\n54\t  cannot have an additional job's pods partially admitted beyond the quota;\n55\t  the additional job is held pending.\n56\t- Quota enforcement at admission works for both PyTorchJob and RayJob\n57\t  workloads.\n58\t- PyTorchJob workloads remain correctly admitted through the existing\n59\t  queueing integration (no regression from quota enforcement).\n60\t- Quota consumption of admitted workloads is attributable per project.\n61\t- Build pipeline for the affected midstream repository is green.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-2 (P0, per-project GPU quota enforced at admission across training job\n66\t  types) — fully covered by this epic.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b01eb154d8d767e0","agent_id":"ae8a577ef2f9405e6","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"6ac54597-be96-4d30-ad4b-1cbf9ba78794","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:11:57.290Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a344af813b4db132","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
