{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99775d2e37cd8825","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E007\n3\ttitle: Implement topology-aware GPU placement preference\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: If Tech Preview node topology discovery is not mature enough\n15\t    this release, HLR-5 placement preference is deferred to a later release and this\n16\t    epic does not run\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Implement topology-aware GPU placement preference\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplements placement preference so multi-node training jobs land on\n39\tGPU-topology-aligned nodes (avoiding, e.g., placements that cross NVLink\n40\tdomains with significant throughput loss) when the cluster exposes topology\n41\tinformation. Gated on the node-topology-discovery maturity investigation:\n42\tthe placement work builds on that capability only after its maturity is\n43\tconfirmed for this release. The placement-preference capability itself\n44\toperates at the scheduler level and is not changed by which admission or\n45\tscheduling mechanism the gang-admission investigation selects; composition\n46\twith all-or-nothing admission is enforced by acceptance criteria that hold\n47\tunder either mechanism.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Add a placement preference for training workloads toward\n52\t  GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster exposes topology information.\n53\t- Build on the node topology discovery capability (currently Tech Preview)\n54\t  only after its maturity investigation confirms it is supported for this\n55\t  release.\n56\t- Compose with the platform's all-or-nothing admission and quota enforcement,\n57\t  whichever admission/scheduling mechanism the gang-admission investigation\n58\t  selects. This composition is verified by acceptance criteria rather than\n59\t  modeled as a blocking dependency, because the placement-preference\n60\t  capability itself is mechanism-independent.\n61\t- Jobs on clusters without topology information continue to schedule normally\n62\t  (preference is best-effort, per HLR-5's \"when the cluster exposes topology\n63\t  information\").\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- On a cluster exposing topology information, a multi-node training job is\n68\t  preferentially placed on topology-aligned nodes rather than crossing\n69\t  topology domains, when such placement is feasible.\n70\t- On a cluster without topology information, jobs schedule without error and\n71\t  without topology preference.\n72\t- Placement preference composes with all-or-nothing admission under either\n73\t  admission mechanism selected by the gang-admission investigation: a job is\n74\t  not partially admitted to achieve better topology alignment.\n75\t- Build pipeline for the affected midstream repository is green.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- HLR-5 (P2, job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n80\t  cluster exposes topology information) — implementation coverage; whether it\n81\t  ships this release is resolved by the topology-discovery maturity\n82\t  investigation.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b01eb154d8d767e0","agent_id":"ae8a577ef2f9405e6","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"33cd41ff-8b95-4067-8aa4-cc090ba2571d","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:12:08.084Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-99775d2e37cd8825","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
