{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbe2a04b250c1064","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008\n3\ttitle: Enable all-or-nothing gang admission using Kueue as-is\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If Kueue's waitForPodsReady semantics prove insufficient at target\n16\t    scale, this configuration-only scope is subsumed into the scheduler-plugin gang-admission\n17\t    implementation (branch B)\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Enable all-or-nothing gang admission using Kueue as-is\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional branch (outcome A): the investigation into gang-admission\n39\tviability concludes that Kueue's existing all-or-nothing admission semantics\n40\t(`waitForPodsReady`) satisfy the requirement for PyTorchJob and RayJob at\n41\ttarget scale. This epic delivers HLR-1 by configuring and enabling Kueue gang\n42\tadmission for the platform's training workload classes, without\n43\tscheduler-plugin work.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Enable/configure Kueue's all-or-nothing admission for multi-node training\n48\t  workloads (PyTorchJob, RayJob) so no partial GPU occupation occurs while\n49\t  waiting for remaining pods.\n50\t- Apply the configuration platform-wide for training workload classes,\n51\t  including the timeout behavior for jobs that cannot be fully admitted.\n52\t- Validate at the target scale established by the gang-admission\n53\t  investigation, including contention scenarios.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A 16-GPU-class multi-node training job holds zero GPUs while waiting for\n58\t  its remaining pods; pods are created only when the full job can be admitted.\n59\t- Both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads are admitted all-or-nothing.\n60\t- Jobs that cannot be fully admitted within the configured timeout are not\n61\t  left partially scheduled.\n62\t- Validation at target scale (per the gating investigation's scale\n63\t  definition) confirms the behavior, including under contention.\n64\t- Existing quota enforcement at admission continues to function with gang\n65\t  admission enabled.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0, multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing) — fully\n70\t  covered by this epic under outcome A.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b01eb154d8d767e0","agent_id":"ae8a577ef2f9405e6","session_id":"0becdb63-9a4f-4908-bf05-bc79d055671f","uuid":"0bb97e32-0e49-464c-8562-a9376c62d1de","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:12:12.090Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbe2a04b250c1064","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
