 1. Do Kueue's gang-admission semantics (waitForPodsReady) satisfy HLR-1 for PyTorchJob/RayJob at target scale, or is scheduler-plugin work needed? | HLR-1 implementation | **Investigation (E001)**. The strategy states the answer \"changes the shape of most implementation work\". Two bounded outcomes → conditional branches (A: Kueue as-is, B: scheduler-plugin/coscheduling). Note: HLR-2 (quota enforcement) is *not* gated — Kueue's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model is GA per architecture context and enforces quota at admission regardless of which gang-scheduling mechanism is selected, so the quota epic proceeds identically under either outcome. |\n| 2. What preemption semantics do reference customers need — full eviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware graceful preemption? | HLR-4 implementation | **Investigation (E002)**. Conflicting field signals + missing checkpoint-overhead benchmark; the answer rewrites the preemption epic's scope. Two bounded outcomes, but the preemption implementation epic exists under either outcome (HLR-4 asks for admin-defined policy; either semantics is a configuration of it) → modeled as a gated main-plan epic with `rewrite` impact rather than branches. |\n| 3. Is Tech Preview node topology discovery mature enough to build HLR-5 on this release? | HLR-5 implementation | **Investigation (E003)**. If immature, HLR-5 is deferred and its epic does not exist this release → gated main-plan epic with `remove` impact. |\n\nNo other unknowns appear in the strategy (no risks table, assumptions, pending\nreviews, or conditional ADRs are present). Implementation details the strategy\nleaves open (exact quota provisioning model, Dashboard view layout, preemption\npolicy schema) are captured as acceptance criteria on the relevant epics, not\nflagged.\n\n## Epic List (main plan)\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E001 | Validate Kueue gang admission for multi-node training jobs at target scale | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E002 | Determine required preemption semantics for training workloads | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E003 | Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 | Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E005 | Surface queue position, quota consumption, and admission state in the Dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 | Implement admin-defined preemption policy for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 | Implement topology-aware GPU placement preference | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n\n### Conditional branch epics (gated by E001, not standalone Jira issues)\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008 | Enable all-or-nothing gang admission using Kueue as-is (HLR-1) | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008 | Implement gang admission with scheduler-plugin coscheduling (HLR-1) | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Investigation: gang admission viability (P0)\"]\n    E002[\"E002 Investigation: preemption semantics (P1)\"]\n    E003[\"E003 Investigation: topology discovery maturity (P2)\"]\n    E004[\"E004 Implementation: per-project GPU quota (P0)\"]\n    E005[\"E005 Implementation: Dashboard queue/quota visibility (P1)\"]\n    E006[\"E006 Implementation: preemption policy (P1)\"]\n    E007[\"E007 Implementation: topology-aware placement (P2)\"]\n    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E008: gang admission via Kueue (P0)\"]\n    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E008: gang admission via scheduler-plugin (P0)\"]\n\n    E001 --> BA\n    E001 --> BB\n    E002 --> E006\n    E003 --> E007\n    E004 --> E005\n```\n\nArrows point from dependency to dependent (\"E001 --> E006\" means E001 must\ncomplete before E006 starts). Branch epics (dashed conceptually) hang off the\nE001 investigation and are not main-plan nodes.\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Gang-admission viability determines whether HLR-1 is configuration-only (branch A). True gate: `rewrite` — if Kueue proves insufficient this scope is subsumed into scheduler-plugin work. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-B-E008 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Same investigation, opposite outcome: scheduler-plugin work exists only if Kueue is insufficient. True gate: `remove` if Kueue suffices. |\n| E002 → E006 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Preemption semantics investigation rewrites the preemption epic's scope (full eviction vs checkpoint-aware). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Topology-discovery maturity decides whether HLR-5 ships this release. True gate: `remove` (defer to later release). |\n| (no edge) E001 → E007 | Rule 3 decision rule, applied per downstream work (removed in revision) | Topology-aware placement composes with whichever admission/scheduling mechanism is selected — the placement-preference capability is scheduler-level and mechanism-independent, mirroring the quota epic's outcome-independence argument. Mechanism composition is enforced by an acceptance criterion on the placement epic (\"composes with all-or-nothing admission under either mechanism\"), not a blocking edge; E007 is gated only by the topology-discovery maturity investigation (E003). |\n| E004 → E005 | 